# config/weewx-onedrive-backup.config — defaults for
# feature-weewx-onedrive-backup (WeeWX database backup to OneDrive).
#
# Most keys here surface on the in-menu Edit Configuration screen via the
# feature's II_EDITABLE_CONFIG: WEEWX_BACKUP_RCLONE_CONF,
# WEEWX_BACKUP_REMOTE_NAME, WEEWX_BACKUP_REMOTE_ROOT, WEEWX_BACKUP_DB_PATH,
# WEEWX_BACKUP_KEEP_DAILY, WEEWX_BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKLY, WEEWX_BACKUP_KEEP_MONTHLY.
# WEEWX_BACKUP_VERIFY stays config-file-only — override it here or in
# overrides/configuration.override.

# Absolute path to the rclone config file on the Pi. rclone's OneDrive
# remote is configured on a desktop machine that has a working browser —
# see scripts/weewx-onedrive-setup.md — and the resulting rclone.conf is
# copied here. The backup systemd timers run as root, so this file must be
# readable by root (the conventional spot is /root/.config/rclone/). The
# install fails with a clear message if the file is absent or the remote
# cannot be listed.
WEEWX_BACKUP_RCLONE_CONF="/root/.config/rclone/rclone.conf"

# Absolute path to the WeeWX SQLite database to back up. The backup always
# uses a DISK copy, never the volatile zram device:
#   - If feature-weewx-database-ram is installed, the runtime script flushes
#     RAM->disk and backs up the SD-card mirror — it reuses just the
#     basename of this path under that feature's PERSIST directory.
#   - Otherwise this path is used as-is (WeeWX's default DB location).
# A future WeeWX-database option that renames or relocates the SQLite file
# only needs this key updated. (A non-SQLite backend would need a different
# backup mechanism entirely.)
WEEWX_BACKUP_DB_PATH="/var/lib/weewx/weewx.sdb"

# How many backup files to keep in each OneDrive tier folder. After every
# upload the tier is pruned to its newest N files; anything older is
# deleted. daily fires once a day, weekly every Sunday, monthly on the 1st —
# so the defaults hold roughly one week / two months / one year of history.
WEEWX_BACKUP_KEEP_DAILY="7"
WEEWX_BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKLY="8"
WEEWX_BACKUP_KEEP_MONTHLY="12"

# Database verification level, run on the snapshot (the exact bytes that
# get uploaded) before each upload:
#   integrity  full PRAGMA integrity_check — thorough (default)
#   quick      PRAGMA quick_check — much faster, still catches most corruption
#   off        skip verification
# The backup runs under a nightly idle-priority timer with a 30-minute
# budget, so even a full integrity_check on a large DB is not a concern;
# drop to "quick" only if you specifically want to shorten each run.
WEEWX_BACKUP_VERIFY="integrity"

# rclone remote name as it appears in rclone.conf — `rclone listremotes`
# prints it with a trailing colon. The setup guide names it "onedrive".
WEEWX_BACKUP_REMOTE_NAME="onedrive"

# Folder path inside OneDrive under which the daily/weekly/monthly tier
# subfolders live. The installer walks and creates each path segment, so a
# typo surfaces before any data is uploaded.
WEEWX_BACKUP_REMOTE_ROOT="Documents-Private/Backups/WeeWX/Database"
